hints:
`parse_kv`: find the first `'='`, reject if it is missing or at position 0, and let `parse_int` judge the rest. `"x=1=2"` fails on its own because `parse_int("1=2")` fails.
```cpp
auto eq = line.find('=');
if (eq == std::string::npos || eq == 0) return std::nullopt;
auto v = parse_int(line.substr(eq + 1));
if (!v) return std::nullopt;
return std::pair{line.substr(0, eq), *v};
```

`parse_config`: a map, a loop, and the if-with-initializer idiom. Assigning through `cfg[k]` gives you "later wins" for free.
```cpp
std::map<std::string, int> cfg;
for (const auto& line : lines)
    if (auto kv = parse_kv(line)) {
        auto [k, v] = *kv;
        cfg[k] = v;
    }
return cfg;
```
